{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>You stretched out Your right hand — the earth swallowed them.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory derived from here that they merited burial as a reward for going up with Joseph for the burial of Jacob our father. And they said in the Midrash: 'right hand' means nothing other than an oath, as it is said (Isaiah 62:8): ״נשבע ה' בימינו״ — 'HaShem has sworn by His right hand.' The explanation is that the sea spewed forth the Egyptians onto dry land, but the dry land refused to receive them, because the Holy One, blessed be He, had cursed the earth when it received the blood of Abel, until the Holy One, blessed be He, swore to it that He would not demand it of it — as it is written: ״נטית ימינך תבלעמו ארץ״ — 'You stretched out Your right hand — the earth swallowed them.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:59:31.061822286Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}